From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:24:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/53] B70-IP-W1: BF16 dense linears as W8A8 int8 on XPU
 (B70_DENSE_INT8=1)

Opt-in. After loading, unquantized linears passing include/exclude regexes are
quantized RTN int8 per output channel; activations int8 per token (native op);
the GEMM is one opaque custom op (torch.ops.vllm.b70_int8_dense_mm): Triton
int8 for M<=64 (decode), oneDNN int8_scaled_mm above (prefill). B70 graph-replay
microbench, rotating weights: 1.5-2.0x faster than BF16 at M=1..4096, ~1.2% rel
err per GEMM. Routers, GDN a/b, indexers, heads, embeddings, HC k-split layers
stay BF16 by default. One summary log line.
